<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pakubuwana I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1719">1719</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Pangeran Puger</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pakubuwana I, earlier Pangeran Puger, was ruler of Mataram from 1704 to 1719. A son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amangkurat-i">Amangkurat I</a>, he claimed the throne against his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amangkurat-iii">Amangkurat III</a> and won it with the help of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-javanese-war-of-succession">First Javanese War of Succession</a>. In return he ceded territory and trade rights on the north coast to the Company.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pakubuwana-i.jpg" alt="Pakubuwana I" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Detail_painting_of_Pangeran_Puger_(later_Pakubuwono_I)_forced_to_execute_his_daughter,_Raden_Ayu_Lembah.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
